An effect written at the root of a file mounts when the program starts.

The effect lowering appends the scope's first settle to the body that holds
the bracket, and for a bracket at the root of a file that is the package body
-- which fyne and gtk4 do not emit: they build their windows from it and drop
every other statement. So the settle was declared, called after a write to the
key, and never called at start, and a root `effect` mounted only once something
changed its key. A `sngl:time` timer at the root is an effect on both, so it
never started (`timer_at_package_root.txtar` committed that fyne golden). A
bubbletea build never had the gap: its body is a pure View, so it calls
`ir.Package.Mounts` from `New` instead, which is what the two now do after
the widget tree they settle into is built.

-- app.sngl --
import go "sngl:language/go"
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        fyne
        gtk4
    }
}

#[go.native("fmt", "fmt.Println")]
func println(s string)

var n = 0

effect(on=n, @mount(k) {
    println("mounted {k}")
})

ui.window {
    ui.text(value="{n}")
    ui.button(text="next", @click {
        n += 1
    })
}
